  "title": "Bonus Farming via Repeated SM-NFT Splitting and Merging",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n\nThe split function in the VotingEscrow contract allows users to divide an existing lock into two separate locks. If the original lock is an SM-NFT, both resulting locks after the split also retain the SM-NFT status. While this may seem reasonable, there is a critical flaw in the bonus handling logic specific to SM-NFTs.\n\nWhen the SM-NFT is split, the split portion is treated as a fresh SM-NFT and the bonus is applied to it. This results in one of the resulting NFTs contain the inflated token balances due to bonuses. \n\nAn attacker can exploit this by repeatedly merging and splitting SM-NFTs—each time receiving additional bonus tokens that should only have been granted once. By looping this process, the attacker effectively farms unearned bonus tokens and inflates their locked balance far beyond their actual deposit, creating a major economic vulnerability in the system.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\n Let's understand the exploit with an example:\n\n- The attacker locks X amount of tokens and chooses the SM-NFT option via the create_lock function.(Also note you get bonus by creating a SMNFT lock.).\n\n```solidity\n function create_lock(uint _value, uint _lock_duration, bool isSMNFT) external nonreentrant returns (uint) {\n       return _create_lock(_value, _lock_duration, msg.sender, isSMNFT); \n    } //@audit if bool isSMNFT = true , SMNFT lock is created . if bool isSMNFT = false , normal lock is created \n```\n- Now they split the NFT into two locks by calling the split function. Heres the [link](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-05-blackhole/blob/92fff849d3b266e609e6d63478c4164d9f608e91/contracts/VotingEscrow.sol#L1147) to the split function\n\n- When they split it, the bonus is added again to the new NFT's which were created.\n\n```solidity\n// Determine the split amount.\n// If the NFT is an SM-NFT, include a synthetic bonus in the split amount.\n// This is the root of the vulnerability: the bonus is re-applied during every split.\nint128 _splitAmount = newLocked.isSMNFT ? \n    int128(int256(_amount + calculate_sm_nft_bonus(_amount))) :  // Vulnerable: Bonus added again\n    int128(int256(_amount));\n\n// Ensure the split amount is non-zero\nrequire(_splitAmount != 0, \"ZV\");\n\n// Ensure the remaining lock after split is not negative\nrequire(newLocked.amount > _splitAmount, \"BIGVAL\");\n\n// Reset the original lock\nlocked[_from] = IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance(0, 0, false, false);\n\n// Save a checkpoint to update state\n_checkpoint(_from, newLocked, IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance(0, 0, false, false));\n\n// Burn the original NFT\n_burn(_from);\n\n// First new NFT after split:\n// Subtract the splitAmount from the original lock and create a new NFT\n// This will hold the remaining part of the lock\nnewLocked.amount -= _splitAmount;\n_tokenId1 = _createSplitNFT(owner, newLocked);\n\n// Second new NFT after split:\n// Assign the (bonus-inflated) _splitAmount to newLocked and create the second NFT\n// This NFT gets a new bonus-inflated amount again\n// Attacker can now repeat this process to keep duplicating bonus\nnewLocked.amount = _splitAmount;\n_tokenId2 = _createSplitNFT(owner, newLocked);\n\n```\n\n- Now they have two NFTs, both with more value than they should have.\n\n- They merge the two NFTs back into one. (Alternatively, instead of merging, they can keep splitting the already split NFTs repeatedly — each time receiving additional bonus — effectively compounding the exploit.\n\n- Then they split the merged NFT again, getting more bonus added.\n\n- By doing this merge and split over and over, the attacker keeps getting free bonus tokens.\n\n- This trick lets the attacker grow their balance way more than they actually put in, giving them unfair power or rewards.\n\n## Impact\n\nUnlimited Bonus Farming: The calculate_sm_nft_bonus function is intended to reward users once when they opt into SM-NFT. However, due to its repeated application on every split, attackers can loop the merge-split process to continually receive unearned bonuses. This causes exponential inflation of locked balances from a fixed initial deposit (e.g., 100 tokens can become 200, 300, etc.).\n\n## Severity Classification\n\n**This issue constitutes a high severity vulnerability because it enables any attacker to artificially inflate their locked balance far beyond their actual token deposit through a simple and repeatable process. By repeatedly merging and splitting SM-NFTs, the attacker can continuously farm bonus tokens, the attacker gains an unfair advantage over honest participants.**\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nRemove the calculate_sm_nft_bonus logic from the split function, even if the lock is marked as an SM-NFT. Users already receive the SM-NFT bonus at the time of lock creation, and reapplying the bonus during a split introduces a critical vulnerability. Allowing the bonus to be added again during each split enables attackers to exploit the system by repeatedly splitting and merging locks to farm unearned bonus tokens.",
